    <h2>Objectives</h2>
    <p>The aims and objectives of the Christian Union are to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Promote growth to maturity in the Christian faith and life among the members of the Union by holding fellowships, prayer meetings, missions, bible studies, seminars, retreats, outreaches and the like, with a view to promote discipleship and leadership development.</li>
        <li>Encourage Christianity as a lifestyle of commitment and heart devotion to Christ, so as to have spiritual, social, physical and academic impact in the Makerere Community.</li>
        <li>Promote and maintain the spiritual interests and safeguard the spiritual welfare of the members from false doctrines and worldly living.</li>
        <li>Foster and promote unity and cooperation among all the evangelical groups of Makerere University.</li>
        <li>Affiliate and create dialogue with the local evangelical churches as well as local/National Para-church organizations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Membership</h2>
    <p>Membership is open to all students of Makerere University who confess faith in Jesus Christ as Lord and Savior and are willing to uphold the Union's Statement of Faith (Doctrinal Basis), objectives, and values.</p>

    <h2>Doctrinal Basis</h2>
    <p>The doctrinal basis of faith of the union is the fundamental truths of Christianity, including:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>The Unity of the Father, Son and the Holy Spirit in the Godhead</li>
        <li>The divine inspiration and entire truthfulness and trustworthiness of the Holy Scriptures as originally given</li>
        <li>The supreme authority of the Holy Scriptures in all matters of faith and conduct</li>
        <li>Redemption from the guilt, penalty, dominion and pollution of sin, solely through the sacrificial death of the Lord Jesus Christ (as our substitute), the incarnate Son of God</li>
        <li>The bodily resurrection of our Lord Jesus Christ from the dead and his ascension to the right hand of God the Father</li>
        <li>The justification of a sinner by the Grace of God through Faith in Jesus Christ alone</li>
        <li>The presence and power of the Holy Spirit in the work of regeneration</li>
        <li>The indwelling and work of the Holy Spirit in the believer</li>
        <li>The unity of all believers in Christ without respect of persons, and without discrimination on account of race, color, nation, social position or otherwise</li>
        <li>The one Holy universal church, which is the body of Christ and to which all true believers belong</li>
        <li>The expectation of the personal return of the Lord Jesus Christ</li>
    </ul>

    <p>This doctrinal base aligns with the core evangelical doctrinal basis of the International Fellowship of Evangelical Students <strong>(IFES)</strong>, the global movement with which FOCUS Uganda and Makerere CU are historically connected. It reflects traditional evangelical Christian teaching that is consistent with the identity of CU as an inter-denominational fellowship centered on the gospel and biblical discipleship.</p>

